This can be accomplished by first determining the offset vector between the hinge and the center of the door. Subsequently, this offset vector can be rotated using the same rotation as the door to establish the correct position of the door relative to the hinge.

Here is a revised implementation:
```kotlin
private _update(deltaTime: number): void {
  this.time += deltaTime;

  const desiredVec3 = this.doorState ? this.doorClosedVec3 : this.doorOpenVec3;

  // Calculate the offset vector between the hinge and the center of the door.
  const doorCenter = this.door?.position.get() || Vec3.zero;
  const hingePosition = this.props.Hinge.position.get();
  const offsetVector = doorCenter.subtract(hingePosition);

  // Calculate the rotation quaternion based on time and desiredVec3.
  const sinTime = Math.sin(this.time);
  const sinVec3 = new Vec3(0, sinTime * 90, 0);
