Consider a custom report type named "Opportunities with Products," which includes fields from both the Opportunity and Product objects. This report type enables viewing of all opportunities along with the products linked to each opportunity. If there is a need to calculate the total value of all products for each opportunity and display this value in the report, one approach could be to create an Apex class with a method that queries data based on the "Opportunities with Products" report type, calculates the total product value for each opportunity, and returns the modified data. Here's a sample code to illustrate this:

