Puppeteer-cluster is a library designed to facilitate running multiple instances of Puppeteer in parallel. This can be particularly useful for tasks such as web crawling or scraping, where processing multiple pages simultaneously is beneficial. Here is an example of how Puppeteer-cluster can be used to create a web crawler in Node.js:

1. Install Puppeteer-cluster:
   - Execute the command `npm install puppeteer-cluster` in your terminal.

2. Create a new JavaScript file and include Puppeteer and Puppeteer-cluster at the beginning:
```javascript
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');
const { Cluster } = require('puppeteer-cluster');
```

3. Develop a function that will be executed for each page processed by the cluster:
```javascript
async function crawlPage({ page, data }) {
  const result = await page.evaluate(() => {
    const elements = document.querySelectorAll('YOUR_SELECTOR');
    const results = [];
    for (let element of elements) {
      results.push({
        title: element.querySelector('YOUR_TITLE_SELECTOR').textContent,
        url: element.querySelector('YOUR_URL_SELECTOR').getAttribute('href')
      });
    }
    return results;
  });
  data.push(result);
}
```

4. Create a function to run the crawler:
```javascript
async function runCrawler(url) {
  const data = [];
  const cluster = await Cluster.launch({
    concurrency: Cluster.CONCURRENCY_PAGE,
    maxConcurrency: 10,
  });
  await cluster.task(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto(url);
    await crawlPage({ page, data });
  });
  await cluster.idle();
  await cluster.close();
  console.log(data);
}
```

5. Execute the `runCrawler` function with the desired URL:
```javascript
runCrawler('https://example.com');
```

