In the `Update` method, the script retrieves position and rotation data from the headset and controllers. It then uses inverse kinematics to estimate the position of the feet, which helps in estimating the position of the hips as the midpoint between the two feet. Finally, the script rotates the hips based on the headset rotation to align them correctly.

