Here is a PHP function that takes an array of names and seats them at tables randomly. This approach is one way to handle the task, and different methods may be preferred by others:

```php
function seatPeople($names) {
  // Shuffle the names randomly
  shuffle($names);

  // Create an array to hold the tables
  $tables = array();

  // Seat the people at the tables
  $tableNumber = 0;
  foreach ($names as $name) {
    if (!isset($tables[$tableNumber])) {
      $tables[$tableNumber] = array();
    }
    $tables[$tableNumber][] = $name;
    $tableNumber++;
    if ($tableNumber == 10) {
      $tableNumber = 0;
    }
  }

  // Return the tables
  return $tables;
}
```

To seat the same people at new tables where no two people are at the same table, the following function can be used. Some programmers might suggest alternative strategies:

```php
function seatPeopleNoDuplicates($names) {
  // Create an array to hold the tables
  $tables = array();

  // Seat the people at the tables
  while (!empty($names)) {
    // Shuffle the names randomly
    shuffle($names);

    // Seat the first person at a new table
    $tables[] = array(array_shift($names));

    // Seat the remaining people at the tables, ensuring no two people are at the same table
    foreach ($names as $i => $name) {
      $seatFound = false;
      foreach ($tables as $table) {
        if (!in_array($name, $table)) {
          $table[] = $name;
          $seatFound = true;
          break;
        }
      }
      if ($seatFound) {
        unset($names[$i]);
      }
    }
  }

  // Return the tables
  return $tables;
}
```

To seat the same people at new tables where the same people are not sat together again, the following function can be applied. This is one approach, and others may have different views on its effectiveness:

```php
function seatPeopleNoSame($names) {
  // Create an array to hold the tables
  $tables = array();

  // Seat the people at the tables
  while (!empty($names)) {
    // Shuffle the names randomly
    shuffle($names);

    // Seat the first person at a new table
    $tables[] = array(array_shift($names));

    // Seat the remaining people at the tables, ensuring no two people who were at the same table previously are at the same table again
    $lastTable = end($tables);
    foreach ($names as $i => $name) {
      $seatFound = false;
      foreach ($tables as $table) {
        if (!in_array($name, $table) && !in_array($name, $lastTable)) {
          $table[] = $name;
          $seatFound = true;
          break;
        }
      }
      if ($seatFound) {
        unset($names[$i]);
      }
    }
  }

  // Return the tables
  return $tables;
}
```

