In this example, chaining is used to set the `href` and `download` attributes of the anchor element one by one. The `attr` method can be called multiple times on the same jQuery object to chain the method calls. 

Some developers suggest that the order of the `attr` method calls does not impact functionality as long as they are all called on the same jQuery object. However, it is often considered a good practice to set the `href` attribute first, followed by the `download` attribute. 

