To display an iframe as a popup, you can utilize JavaScript or jQuery to create a modal window and place the iframe within it. Here is an example using jQuery:

```html
<button id="openBtn">Open iframe</button>

<script>
$(document).ready(function(){
    $("#openBtn").click(function(){
        $("#iframeModal").modal();
    });
});
</script>

<div id="iframeModal" class="modal">
  <iframe src="http://example.com"></iframe>
</div>
```

In this example, a button with the ID "openBtn" is used to initiate the opening of the modal window. When the button is clicked, the jQuery code will activate a modal window with the ID "iframeModal" and display the iframe inside it.

You can apply CSS to style the modal window and iframe according to your preferences to achieve the desired popup appearance.

There are several potential reasons why the modal window is showing scrollbars when it should not. One possibility is that the modal window or the iframe itself has a fixed height and width, and the content within the iframe is larger than the dimensions of the modal window. In this case, it may be helpful to ensure that the modal window and the iframe have a responsive design, allowing them to adjust to the size of the content.

Another potential cause could be that the CSS of the modal window or the iframe is not configured to hide the scrollbars. Some suggest adding the following code to your CSS to hide the scrollbars:
```
#iframeModal {
  overflow: hidden;
}

#iframeModal iframe {
  overflow: hidden;
}
```
This approach aims to ensure that the modal window and the iframe do not display any scrollbars, even if the content inside the iframe is larger than the dimensions of the modal window.

Another suggestion is to set the height and width of the iframe to 100% to fill the modal window:
```
<iframe src="http://example.com" style="height:100%; width:100%;"></iframe>
```
It may also be beneficial to check if the iframe's content is responsive. If it is not, some recommend making it responsive by using CSS media queries.

If these solutions do not resolve the issue, further troubleshooting may be necessary.

