@Override
public int partition(Object key) {
    // Implement your custom partitioning logic here.
    // For example, you can use the hashCode of the key:
    int hashCode = key.hashCode();

    // Ensure the result is non-negative and falls within the range of partition count:
    return Math.abs(hashCode % partitions);
}
```
The `partition()` method takes an object key and applies custom partitioning logic. In this example, the hashCode of the key is used, but different logic can be applied based on specific requirements. The result is adjusted to be non-negative and within the partition count range.

