@Override
public List<List<ClusterNode>> assignPartitions(AffinityFunctionContext ctx) {
    List<List<ClusterNode>> assignments = new ArrayList<>(partitions);

    for (int i = 0; i < partitions; i++) {
        assignments.add(new ArrayList<>());
    }

    // Iterate over all nodes and assign partitions to them
    for (int part = 0; part < partitions; part++) {
        Collection<ClusterNode> nodes = ctx.currentTopologySnapshot();

        for (ClusterNode node : nodes) {
            // Implement custom logic to determine if a node should have the partition
            if (shouldAssignPartitionToNode(node, part)) {
                assignments.get(part).add(node);
            }
        }
    }

    return assignments;
}
```
This method returns a list of lists, where each list contains the `ClusterNode`s assigned to a specific partition. Users are encouraged to implement their own logic to decide which nodes should be assigned to each partition.

2. To implement the `shouldAssignPartitionToNode()` method:
